    "Durotar's coast is red rock and warm shallows. Trolls of the Echo Isles say the mackerel run thickest when the tide carries the smell of the islands' cooking fires.",  -- 362
    "The lakes of Mulgore are small, clear and patient. The tauren fish them the way they do everything else: slowly, and with thanks.",  -- 363
    "Every oasis in the Barrens is a meeting place. Whatever drinks there by day, something swims under it by night.",  -- 364
    "The pools of Teldrassil lie in the shade of one tree. Night elf anglers swear the fish there have never seen the sun and do not miss it.",  -- 365
    "Darkshore's water is grey, cold and full of wrecks. Half of what bites off Auberdine has made a home in somebody's lost cargo.",  -- 366
    "The rivers of Ashenvale run under leaves older than most kingdoms. The fish are quick, and the sentinels are quicker to ask what you are doing there.",  -- 367
    "Down among the Thousand Needles the water is scarce and jealously kept. A fish from here has earned its place.",  -- 368
    "Stonetalon's lakes sit high and cold between the peaks. The goblins would have drained them by now if the fishing were not so good.",  -- 369
    "The coast of Desolace is bones and grey surf. Something down there has a taste for both.",  -- 370
    "Feralas is green all the way down to the waterline. Its rivers are deep, warm and very much alive.",  -- 371
    "Nobody is sure where Dustwallow's land stops and its water begins. Fish from the shore, and count your toes afterwards.",  -- 372
    "Steamwheedle Port has the only water worth the name in Tanaris. The goblins will sell you the right to fish it, twice if you let them.",  -- 373
    "Under Azshara's bright bay lies a drowned city. Old anglers say the big ones live in what used to be its gardens.",  -- 374
    "The pools of Felwood glow, and not in a good way. What still swims in them is stubborn beyond reason.",  -- 375
    "The hot springs and tar-rimmed lakes of Un'Goro have kept things the rest of the world forgot. Some of them bite.",  -- 376
    "Lake Elune'ara in Moonglade is as calm as a held breath. The druids ask only that you take no more than you will eat.",  -- 377
    "Silithus is sand, wind and the sound of wings. If you have found water to fish here, tell no one.",  -- 378
    "The lakes of Winterspring freeze at the edges and steam in the middle. The fish there are fat for the cold and worth the walk.",  -- 379
    "The pools of Orgrimmar are fished by peons with nothing better to do and by old grunts who say the same. Both tell you the big one got away.",  -- 380
    "A fish from the ponds of Thunder Bluff has lived its whole life a long way above the plains. It seems calm about it.",  -- 381
    "Darnassus keeps its waters as carefully as its temples. The fish have grown used to being admired.",  -- 382
    "The lakes of the Alterac Mountains are snowmelt, and the ogres and the Syndicate fish them when no one is looking.",  -- 383
    "Arathi's shores have seen more armies than anglers. The fish have long since stopped caring whose banner flies above the water.",  -- 384
    "The Badlands are dust from one end to the other. A bite here is a small miracle; treat it as one.",  -- 385
    "The coast of the Blasted Lands is red, scoured and quiet. Whatever lives in that surf has learned to live with a great deal.",  -- 386
    "The lakes of Tirisfal lie still under a sickly sky. The Forsaken fish them out of habit; the dead do not eat much, but they remember liking it.",  -- 387
    "Silverpine's long coast is all mist and pine shadow. The fishing is good, which is the one cheerful thing anyone says about the place.",  -- 388
    "The rivers of the Western Plaguelands still run, though not clean. What you pull from them, look at twice.",  -- 389
    "Few people fish the Eastern Plaguelands, and fewer say so. The water keeps what the plague left of it.",  -- 390
    "Hillsbrad's river and its long southern shore have fed both sides of every quarrel fought over them.",  -- 391
    "The Hinterlands keep their lakes high among the trees, where the Wildhammer dwarves fish from gryphon-back when they think no one can see.",  -- 392
    "The lakes of Dun Morogh are ringed with ice most of the year. A dwarf will cut a hole, sit down with a pint and call it a good day whatever bites.",  -- 393
    "The Searing Gorge has lava where other lands have rivers. Bring something to drink instead.",  -- 394
    "The Burning Steppes are ash and embers. If the water here gives you anything at all, it will be hot.",  -- 395
    "Every child in Elwynn learns to fish at Crystal Lake or Stone Cairn. The smallfish there have been outwitting them for generations.",  -- 396
    "Deadwind Pass has little water and less welcome. What is in the pools below Karazhan is best left there.",  -- 397
    "The river along Duskwood's edge is black at any hour. The fish do not seem to mind the dark; the anglers do.",  -- 398
    "The Loch is the pride of Loch Modan, held back by the great Stonewrought Dam. Dwarves measure a fishing story against it, and the Loch usually wins.",  -- 399
    "Lake Everstill in Redridge is as pretty as a painting and fished from every dock in Lakeshire. The townsfolk know each good spot and will not tell you one.",  -- 400
    "From its jungle rivers to the wild southern cape, Stranglethorn has the richest water on the continent. Booty Bay's anglers hold a tournament over it, and nearly all of them cheat.",  -- 401
    "The Swamp of Sorrows is green water under green trees. The fish taste of mud, and the locals like them that way.",  -- 402
    "Westfall's fields failed, but its coast did not. The folk who stayed live off the long grey shore.",  -- 403
    "The Wetlands are well named. Menethil Harbor's docks are the driest place to fish them, and the crocolisks know it.",  -- 404
    "The canals of Stormwind are fished by children, pensioners and at least one member of the nobility in disguise. Nobody asks what else is in the canals.",  -- 405
    "The Forlorn Cavern holds Ironforge's one quiet pool. Old dwarves fish it for hours and never say a word.",  -- 406
    "The canals of the Undercity run a green that has nothing to do with algae. The Forsaken who fish them are not doing it for supper.",  -- 407
    "The first fish most anglers ever land, and bright enough that they remember it.",  -- 408
    "Slick, quick and common along every warm coast. It is better grilled than its name suggests.",  -- 409
    "All mouth, and happiest in water you would not drink.",  -- 410
    "Small, toothy and fearless. A shoal of them is said to have chased a bear out of the Loch.",  -- 411
    "A flash of colour under the surf. Sailors count one on the line as luck for the voyage.",  -- 412
    "A patient bottom-feeder with whiskers like a dwarven elder.",  -- 413
    "No one eats it twice. Alchemists buy every one they can get.",  -- 414
    "Its fins glow like banked coals, and the oil pressed from it burns nearly as well.",  -- 415
    "Armoured like a small shield. The meat inside is worth the trouble.",  -- 416
    "Something in the water near the Wailing Caverns changed it. Eating one may change you as well, for a while.",  -- 417
    "River folk say a meal of it clears the mind. It is the swimming upstream that makes it wise.",  -- 418
    "Older, larger and wiser than its cousin, which did not keep it off your hook.",  -- 419
    "A hard fighter from warm southern seas, and a favourite on every tavern board from Booty Bay to Gadgetzan.",  -- 420
    "Its brow shines like true mithril. More than one miner has tried to smelt one.",  -- 421
    "Its scales boil down into an oil that makes the skin as hard as rock. It prefers the night.",  -- 422
    "Polished like a parade breastplate, and nearly as heavy.",  -- 423
